}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17751a3b-ed4b-5966-a450-330460c02715" :question/math-academy-id "q-50139" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-10.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-10\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-10x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-10x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-10\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D \\\\  & =-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a745d53-2adc-5935-a97d-5a586599fa37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095731} {:answer/id #uuid "f4387418-5075-52c7-b685-924f2791a4be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095732} {:answer/id #uuid "035eddbc-75fb-53ba-bc61-c5e0c4f3f025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095733} {:answer/id #uuid "12887777-c8a6-5e16-bf30-ed290559c1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095734} {:answer/id #uuid "7a68fbfe-8f1c-512a-8cc2-1b00fe18af49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095735}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5a4615-20d2-563a-8738-3f3905aa1549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae67e9eb-7a6a-5f1f-9633-a869be11af9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398897} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9d1539-56f7-56d2-9de6-1e9901343c60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398898} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ac46a-1dd6-5423-b497-fd6f6d213a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398899} {:answer/id #uuid "bd19773a-598c-5d4a-9935-ec0892a47ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398900} {:answer/id #uuid "89be7220-c09b-594d-8bff-c3a06f0b9221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ac46a-1dd6-5423-b497-fd6f6d213a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398899} :answer-field/id #uuid "30eeac9f-d833-5bc8-934f-4097337092f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e04bc45-f34f-56fc-9a0e-8643597c4852" :question/math-academy-id "q-50148" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222d3811-c9d6-5e7d-b85c-95aa3edf1f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250846} {:answer/id #uuid "2aeffcd6-4797-59ec-860f-11aa268d3482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250918} {:answer/id #uuid "65573541-1d72-5f2c-8753-db5f49766c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251383} {:answer/id #uuid "849fa2e5-06fb-57df-930c-0b02e73c0378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251665} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1f009d-922c-586a-8478-6e8b8c14b8c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aeffcd6-4797-59ec-860f-11aa268d3482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250918} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdcccacb-a603-583d-bd6c-044e60d286f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31249dfd-dd0f-51ef-9508-c411dcb82eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119038" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{-2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int {e}^{-2x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+C \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{-2x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a7a8ec6-3a7f-59a8-a36a-57b3c0e72d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251298} {:answer/id #uuid "7c79b537-ac7c-5f96-ac1d-d1860fe46a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251588} {:answer/id #uuid "bf97146c-f829-59ef-a419-71c2a32c9365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252244} {:answer/id #uuid "caaff75b-db1f-5d6d-9954-596535269be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252349} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a50774-5155-52c7-ab4f-ad427a04fce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a7a8ec6-3a7f-59a8-a36a-57b3c0e72d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251298} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dba1b47-1418-53b5-8e0b-75806451ee28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39f64cb7-5a70-5fc4-8565-289e61a98a66" :question/math-academy-id "q-119041" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-8(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52771b76-d1b4-51e6-ab25-23d4a36b8b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=16{e}^{x/2}+{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251227} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ba7691-e0f5-58b0-8306-ebfe9995ce2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252144} {:answer/id #uuid "d52fa157-a79b-5633-8056-0ad742ff72b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=8{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252440} {:answer/id #uuid "dad3e85e-1ff8-5404-b11a-42ecf755a4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252477} {:answer/id #uuid "e75f3c4e-0901-518a-8832-fdbd533170dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=32{e}^{x/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dad3e85e-1ff8-5404-b11a-42ecf755a4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252477} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc11b9f-979a-5428-873c-d6f95fed2f3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f306795-58e9-56b9-bfb8-50791b341767" :question/math-academy-id "q-119042" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6x=8{e}^{x/2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{x/2}-6x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8{e}^{x/2}-6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(2{e}^{x/2})-6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =16\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =16(2{e}^{x/2})-3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cc8ac7-5e09-54ce-b6d3-e159d67ab8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250861} {:answer/id #uuid "5901205a-e2f9-52f3-b94e-a09bbbbe0521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251285} {:answer/id #uuid "60767b47-bf28-5927-9170-56b9e257c34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251342} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4e1b67-45cb-51ac-a61f-ee18bbb149b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252358} {:answer/id #uuid "f4155827-e220-55c0-a8b5-d48c90df5a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc4e1b67-45cb-51ac-a61f-ee18bbb149b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252358} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb1d879-87da-5436-bd2a-6290c0abb0e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5323a95-ccb4-5698-8e94-ec2b6a694be3" :question/math-academy-id "q-119043" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061e9049-685a-5e57-b12d-6b56030be323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250602} {:answer/id #uuid "42b59196-b9a8-573b-be83-9fd902357365" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={2}^{x}{ln}^{2}⁡2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251109} {:answer/id #uuid "b5960315-6cae-5802-922d-5b341c99ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252150} {:answer/id #uuid "c18c981b-dd26-58f1-bd40-912972cd4a5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252261} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e95291-17f3-571b-b000-bb1e43ebce08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061e9049-685a-5e57-b12d-6b56030be323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250602} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27e7bd7-eaed-55b0-916c-a3dd3a5a5d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f9dee74-c92e-5523-b157-7ba038c745c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119044" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{2}^{x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3120f347-6512-51ba-8814-9e94e5b4f3e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330382} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce95280-683d-5e12-8dc4-4bd3c4dab2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330490} {:answer/id #uuid "3f867192-f0f3-5837-8919-076f5a3bf835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330514} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3c8989-f6d0-5647-ba9e-eebb2011d570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332030} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd989d0-88b5-5bdf-841b-6beef220f5ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ce95280-683d-5e12-8dc4-4bd3c4dab2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330490} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc205ab-aa57-5042-9e55-6ce79c5b03ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d572743-1005-5db1-a849-a7030811290a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50146" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-4(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-2(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4239f824-0cdb-56c2-b03e-ba26979ede69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{5}\\,{x}^{3/2}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345918} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b8e6e-4ec7-58f9-81fa-5762778dd80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346028} {:answer/id #uuid "517c9cdb-fafc-50c3-8c25-73b1c9f3a696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346052} {:answer/id #uuid "8b73bf1b-fafc-5923-a918-fb2d34e27d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346559} {:answer/id #uuid "995de1a6-1b5d-505e-b32d-431f2c275661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}\\,{x}^{3/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b8e6e-4ec7-58f9-81fa-5762778dd80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346028} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14bd67c-bf99-5b34-a9b6-546acd076bc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347887}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49effcbe-cf5f-52f7-9899-b28e9803c299" :question/math-academy-id "q-79554" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\sqrt{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}\\,{x}^{5/2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\,{x}^{5/2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2339eddd-c520-53fc-835c-406bf5642b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398202} {:answer/id #uuid "6cfc929f-0e67-5e47-80b6-d2949d1be4b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{4}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398203} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd5ffc9-d74f-592b-a383-53ba3803f136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398204} {:answer/id #uuid "395e4984-cf1d-534b-b01f-09b03aa00ba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4{x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398205} {:answer/id #uuid "796c5808-234b-5385-a5e5-513d3b55563c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=5{x}^{4}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dd5ffc9-d74f-592b-a383-53ba3803f136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398204} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7d8f65-a93b-5daa-b8fa-34a0b4f4a5ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f503fbb-9abb-5178-8aa2-5b5187c150ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-119039" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=20{x}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =20\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+C \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+Cx+D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "badd1b57-14e7-5b56-b3e2-4f76bf483962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399338} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc1b791-33fe-5cbe-8db2-7cec317b3415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399339} {:answer/id #uuid "9947a22d-6748-5635-9bff-c054c9d5412e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399340} {:answer/id #uuid "a32a5598-4875-50b4-a207-219749ce447a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399341} {:answer/id #uuid "39ea83b4-6e8e-5133-9645-9dd52053a38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "badd1b57-14e7-5b56-b3e2-4f76bf483962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399338} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d542a7-e1e6-5040-8811-6896030adc94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99338d6e-762d-5e46-924e-c9b8ff055bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-99009" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24f127e6-1306-5a2b-a3d3-e1cfe2de5c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496444} {:answer/id #uuid "5dab8531-5053-5b1b-960d-22107ac03ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496456} {:answer/id #uuid "a757570a-5b0a-50a9-bc98-ac563d9d1ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496472} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ca0a9f-4c7c-5392-b936-b70a824ebe7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496482} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1b0f73-2efc-5389-b2ce-f608d80d53f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - 12 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a757570a-5b0a-50a9-bc98-ac563d9d1ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496472} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddb49e73-0d27-5a15-86c6-4ce6a587bf67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "035ced66-4ab9-5d2d-a65a-0b6c4095543d" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(6 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((6)\\int \\left(e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((6)\\left(- 2 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C - 12 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C - 12 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((-12)\\int \\left(e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-12)\\left(- 2 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b7a9ee-05d2-5e22-9972-601b4fb37512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496443} {:answer/id #uuid "98586e82-d740-5cdf-8e68-aec82060ba46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496467} {:answer/id #uuid "a45dd023-ac47-5719-bfa2-a56d75067b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496471} {:answer/id #uuid "e06fa046-2cc1-520d-ad5d-71c843cfdecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2} - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496480} {:answer/id #uuid "ef279cf5-32e4-53ca-b8a9-ca1692cb44ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D - \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17b7a9ee-05d2-5e22-9972-601b4fb37512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496443} :answer-field/id #uuid "f54355e5-1536-513f-be27-f9963dda5050" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a8c21f0-1469-51c6-8b1e-9df019a179b7" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 12 \\cdot 2^{x} + 20 x + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 3 \\cdot 2^{x} + 5 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- 3 \\cdot 2^{x} + 5 x + 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((5)\\int \\left(x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-3)\\int \\left(2^{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((2)\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((5)\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right)) + ((-3)\\left(\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)) + ((2)\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right))+C \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} + C + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2} - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} + C + \\frac{5 x^{2}}{2} - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((\\frac{5}{2})\\int \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((- \\frac{3}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}})\\int \\left(2^{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-4)\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((\\frac{5}{2})\\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right)) + ((- \\frac{3}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}})\\left(\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}}\\right)) + ((-4)\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}^{2}} + C x + D + \\frac{5 x^{3}}{6} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496457 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a018671-33dd-5e1e-a486-47ea10f91d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496446} {:answer/id #uuid "96e035ed-98be-559e-afe9-4fdf3c466757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{7 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + 4 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496465} {:answer/id #uuid "98d9400f-9d5a-5d32-9ef8-18683c25276d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496468} {:answer/id #uuid "9d88d181-065b-5b99-9c3d-def935f9acf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496470} {:answer/id #uuid "ab12cfcf-d837-5893-98cc-7bf52f85922b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{x^{3}}{6} + \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} + 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d88d181-065b-5b99-9c3d-def935f9acf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496470} :answer-field/id #uuid "c862d365-4036-51de-9a7d-af7d82638b2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64d2112b-6455-564b-a00e-e1e0242afaf1" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 2 x + 14 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 16 e^{- 2 x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- x + 7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 8 e^{- 2 x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- x + 7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 8 e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-1)\\int \\left(x\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-8)\\int \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((7)\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((-1)\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right)) + ((-8)\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right)) + ((7)\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{7 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + 4 e^{- 2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C - \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{7 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} + 4 e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((- \\frac{1}{2})\\int \\left(x^{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((4)\\int \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((\\frac{7}{2})\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((- \\frac{1}{2})\\left(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right)) + ((4)\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right)) + ((\\frac{7}{2})\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D - \\frac{x^{3}}{6} - \\frac{7 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4} - 2 e^{- 2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d92b48-ec79-52ab-a285-33d507f81dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496449} {:answer/id #uuid "7b45ba37-d4e1-534a-a901-557a1c17a7d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496460} {:answer/id #uuid "8a313bb8-d9a1-533b-b56d-8892fa941211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496464} {:answer/id #uuid "be37962b-6efd-515c-a571-a13f146db634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496475} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa554b3-4a68-5807-bb3b-0cf90a40cca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47d92b48-ec79-52ab-a285-33d507f81dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496449} :answer-field/id #uuid "477df44a-11a1-5101-aade-bfbe97b75816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76795e9c-6c55-5ca7-a4fc-d6d343e2c852" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- e^{- 2 x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-1)\\int \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((-1)\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((\\frac{1}{2})\\int \\left(e^{- 2 x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((\\frac{1}{2})\\left(- \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "431e3f50-9697-534f-b81d-9a9818b4b4f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{x^{6}}{15} + \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} - \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496447} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7877ce-f2f4-5a6c-bc6c-70bfe99570ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496452} {:answer/id #uuid "84ba00bd-ae03-5a27-bcc9-49ecdcd0d954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} - 2 x^{4} + \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496462} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2b08ce-e008-5a63-b350-3f4ff774087b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D - \\frac{x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496469} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b497df-f5b4-5a27-8162-1ef52bf3b6b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x - \\frac{x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f7877ce-f2f4-5a6c-bc6c-70bfe99570ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496452} :answer-field/id #uuid "553b156e-b41f-5b74-a709-a7550e26968b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b9b05e0-1d53-595d-87f6-fcb0ea344f67" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n3\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 6 x^{4} - 24 x^{3} - 6 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 2 x^{4} - 8 x^{3} - 2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- 2 x^{4} - 8 x^{3} - 2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-8)\\int \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-2)\\int \\left(x^{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-2)\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((-8)\\left(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right)) + ((-2)\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}\\right)) + ((-2)\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} - 2 x^{4} + \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} - 2 x^{4} + \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((-2)\\int \\left(x^{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((- \\frac{2}{5})\\int \\left(x^{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((\\frac{2}{3})\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-2)\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}\\right)) + ((- \\frac{2}{5})\\left(\\frac{x^{6}}{6}\\right)) + ((\\frac{2}{3})\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D - \\frac{x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{2 x^{5}}{5} + \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16c97bc6-f60d-54c4-b7a0-0109b8b665a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{3 x^{4}}{2} + 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} - 12 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496442} {:answer/id #uuid "52effbc3-75dd-51c0-8b3c-224c3cd54fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496453} {:answer/id #uuid "706eaced-8e8c-52e2-bfea-e59cc1590246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496458} {:answer/id #uuid "96fe4e2b-4cff-525b-8ad1-4de8638750aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} - 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496466} {:answer/id #uuid "d82f188a-2305-57a9-8ca5-cb043c85d10d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D + \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "706eaced-8e8c-52e2-bfea-e59cc1590246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496458} :answer-field/id #uuid "e387b32c-b692-5d4f-ab95-49c805f1cfd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "adfc6c39-9c84-5054-86dc-08ce214860eb" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=24 x^{3} - 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6 x^{3} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 6 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(6 x^{3} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 6 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((6)\\int \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((6)\\int \\left(e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-2)\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((6)\\left(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right)) + ((6)\\left(- 2 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)) + ((-2)\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C + \\frac{3 x^{4}}{2} + 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} - 12 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C + \\frac{3 x^{4}}{2} + 4 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} - 12 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((\\frac{3}{2})\\int \\left(x^{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-12)\\int \\left(e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((4)\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((\\frac{3}{2})\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}\\right)) + ((-12)\\left(- 2 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}\\right)) + ((4)\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D + \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} + 8 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{x}{2} \\right)} + 24 e^{- \\frac{x}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186496486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481097fd-f9ae-55d3-8f5c-722e350c0b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=D - \\frac{4 x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496450} {:answer/id #uuid "49e876e9-eec7-5526-ad6f-32142b42b519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x - \\frac{4 x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496451} {:answer/id #uuid "55ca0676-4986-53de-8bfe-c98830d32367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{4 x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496455} {:answer/id #uuid "8922d260-2923-5acd-b341-65d16531156a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D + \\frac{4 x^{6}}{15} + \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} + \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496463} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2e2fff-1806-5d13-b4de-becd24629d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{8 x^{5}}{5} - \\frac{3 x^{4}}{2} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55ca0676-4986-53de-8bfe-c98830d32367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=C x + D - \\frac{4 x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496455} :answer-field/id #uuid "fad2a396-3caa-5aaa-b023-a60543b5a4e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f11b903b-958d-5c91-a4bb-2c7b220c4cab" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 16 x^{4} - 12 x^{3} + 4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=- 8 x^{4} - 6 x^{3} + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(- 8 x^{4} - 6 x^{3} + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =((-6)\\int \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((-8)\\int \\left(x^{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((2)\\int \\left(\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =((-6)\\left(\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right)) + ((-8)\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}\\right)) + ((2)\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right))+C \\\\  & =C - \\frac{8 x^{5}}{5} - \\frac{3 x^{4}}{2} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(C - \\frac{8 x^{5}}{5} - \\frac{3 x^{4}}{2} + \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =((- \\frac{3}{2})\\int \\left(x^{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((- \\frac{8}{5})\\int \\left(x^{5}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x) + ((1)\\int \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x)+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =((- \\frac{3}{2})\\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}\\right)) + ((- \\frac{8}{5})\\left(\\frac{x^{6}}{6}\\right)) + ((1)\\left(- \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\right))+Cx+D \\\\  & =C x + D - \\frac{4 x^{6}}{15} - \\frac{3 x^{5}}{10} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}]}
